{"title":"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A dish contains 100 candies. Juan removes candies from the dish each day and no candies are added to the dish. On day 1, Juan removes 1 candy. On day 2, Juan removes 2 candies. On each day that follows, Juan removes 1 more candy than he removed on the previous day. After day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, Juan has removed a total of at least 64 candies. What is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Guessing_Reasonable_Values.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Guessing_Reasonable_Values)\">Solution 1 (Guessing Reasonable Values)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Guessing Reasonable Values)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the total number of candies that have been removed after day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/30099cf7b1d670e63c894aaed201ecc57d8a3cdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\cdots + (n - 1) + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"20\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55fa61f6f77bd5e9dc733cb36e4c7372130dfb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa17013a449147f7545eaf8c6efd44b5b9fa2034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/0175b4a65742a52e418d064454a944db85583b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/9/47979892a3627658a897c0c6c6dd047c41315533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then this would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dda6b0181c4ac5020698523e517441ec961a0b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11 \\times 12}{2} = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. We then see that the first time that Juan has removed a total of at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> candies is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a262cc510473960b63fa531ec286b5009bc8d6cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"66\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC\" title=\"2020 CIMC\">2020 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2020 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062917\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 97/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1289/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 140/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2004/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.015      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    7.015      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37166:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062917 and revision id 287064. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}